B1McA&oe=6B10488D"}, {"file_name": "spacemr-screenshot-5.png", "id": "1839889403690806", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/908839705_1839889407024139_4577311004107305669_n.png?_nc_cat=101&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=xteogTrnbcgQ7kNvwHxUKeN&_nc_oc=AdqAdiINeqfOh0CQtPt1ivI9CQV6c3SsjPJjkxNYNRVOvI8FiQ3-lDfiE26oFiwQTys&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f30f&oh=00_AQWcwT3dr0FvnMbQv4r8Mu75Y0hBuPZBzReelYw3eXEpuA&oe=6B10570A"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "DUET Space Lab MR", "keywords": ["space", "planets", "astronomy", "education", "science"], "long_description": "DUET Space Lab MR brings the Solar System into your classroom or home through the Quest's passthrough.\n\n\u2022 The Sun, the planets and their main moons, with NASA surface maps, moving in their real order around the Sun.\n\u2022 The Solar System appears in front of you, floating in your room, and you can look at it from any side. Move it with the grip button, or bring it back in front of you from the panel under it; make it bigger or smaller with the thumbstick or the \u2212 and + buttons.\n\u2022 Point at a planet and pull the trigger, or pinch with your fingers, to open its facts: size, distance from the Sun, length of its year and its moons.\n\u2022 Works with Touch controllers or with bare hands.\n\u2022 Speed up or slow down the planets.\n\u2022 Narration and text in English or Hindi.\n\u2022 Needs the internet the first time it opens; after that it works offline.\n\nFree to use: no school code and no account needed.", "short_description": "See the Solar System in your own room: the Sun, planets and moons float around you in mixed reality. Open any planet for its facts, in English or Hindi."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://ashutoshduet.github.io/duet-lms-media/space/privacy.html", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "DUET Power", "